    netWorth: "$5.6B", era: "Value & Growth",
    bio: "Joe Lewis was born in a working-class neighborhood in London's East End above a pub that his parents ran. He left school at 15 to help run the family catering business. In the 1970s, he expanded into currency trading, using profits from the restaurants to fund his positions. He developed a reputation for making bold directional bets on currencies, often holding positions for months.\n\nLewis's defining trade came in September 1992, alongside George Soros. He had been building massive short positions against the British pound, convinced the UK could not maintain its ERM peg. While Soros gets the credit for \"breaking the Bank of England,\" Lewis was reportedly trading in similar size, earning an estimated $1.8 billion from the trade. It remains one of the largest single profits ever made by an individual trader.\n\nAfter the pound trade, Lewis moved to the Bahamas for tax purposes and has maintained an extremely low public profile ever since. He owns the Tottenham Hotspur football club and has made significant investments in golf resorts, restaurants, and currency trading. He rarely gives interviews and is known for his privacy, letting his trading results speak for themselves.",
