    bio: "Vijay Kedia was born in Kolkata, India, into a family of stockbrokers. His grandfather and father were both members of the Calcutta Stock Exchange. Kedia started trading at age 19 after his father's death, but he had no formal education in finance. His early years were difficult \u2014 he made money, lost it, and made it again, learning through painful experience.\n\nKedia's breakthrough came when he shifted from trading to investing. He developed a simple philosophy: find small, high-quality companies with honest management, strong growth potential, and scalable businesses. Buy them when they're undiscovered, and hold them for years as they grow into large companies. He called these \"multibaggers\" \u2014 stocks that return multiple times the initial investment.\n\nHis most famous multibaggers include Atul Auto, Cera Sanitaryware, and Aegis Logistics, each returning 10x to 100x his initial investment. Kedia is known for his thorough research process, visiting companies, meeting management teams, and analyzing businesses from the ground up. He has become one of India's most respected individual investors and a vocal advocate for the potential of India's small-cap companies.",
